{"id": "EUVD-2026-59398", "enisaUuid": "9af490a6-7638-383a-9a2b-8681797460c5", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nRDMA/bnxt_re: Free CQ toggle page after firmware teardown\n\nFree the toggle page only after firmware teardown completes so that\nan NQ interrupt arriving during bnxt_qplib_destroy_cq() won't write\nthe toggle value to an already-freed page. Move free_page() after\nbnxt_qplib_destroy_cq.", "datePublished": "2026-08-15T05:57:31", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:45:06", "baseScore": 8.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:C/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8a8d69a01bda1fec9b07b5559be2b6ed45b1e974", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/33aed3ba04aa56eeeb876935896aa6530c46640e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b193854675ecad43b4d69c304c1b6a90b206cc99", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/bb45e06f9914ca64ac95341a80a0c20bb8dd46a9"], "aliases": ["GHSA-2899-vqg2-g66r", "CVE-2026-72499"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.18, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "11a6ca75-27c4-33bb-bc9d-1ad1acbe6749", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e275919d96693c5ca964b20d73a33d52a7e57f04 <bb45e06f9914ca64ac95341a80a0c20bb8dd46a9"}, {"id": "8489f83b-a588-30cd-9064-c3143c76fb58", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e275919d96693c5ca964b20d73a33d52a7e57f04 <b193854675ecad43b4d69c304c1b6a90b206cc99"}, {"id": "8eb073af-1bb1-3888-a562-17915d87f940", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "99d764ee-6a05-36f0-94ee-e99059c80866", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1.5"}, {"id": "a95b7a5b-cdd2-327f-ad0b-80942434e4e3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "b021d264-c623-3aad-9d20-da37b83549c7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vend